    <briefdescription>
<para>Abstract contract for the request-facing CRUDS handlers exposed for every entity type. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Declares five operations (Create, Read, Update, Delete, Search), each in a synchronous callback form and in a <computeroutput>drogon::Task</computeroutput> coroutine form. Implementations (see <ref refid="classEntityController" kindref="compound">EntityController</ref>) are expected to parse and validate <computeroutput>data</computeroutput>, authorize the action with <computeroutput>requester</computeroutput>, construct the entity and delegate persistence to the lower-level <ref refid="classController" kindref="compound">Controller</ref>. The callback is <computeroutput><ref refid="callback_8hpp_1a46d97763fde9c175df21fc9b8f73b1d3" kindref="member">CALLBACK_</ref></computeroutput> = <computeroutput>std::function&lt;void(int, const std::string&amp;)&gt;</computeroutput>: implementations invoke it once with an HTTP status code and a response body, including on error paths.</para>
<para>The interface itself does not own or store any state; derived controllers supply the collaborators. The lifetime of <computeroutput>callback</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>requester</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>data</computeroutput> (and of the owning controller) must extend until the coroutine variants complete, because they are borrowed by the coroutine frame. <simplesect kind="note"><para>The <computeroutput>const <ref refid="structRequester" kindref="compound">Requester</ref>&amp;&amp;</computeroutput> parameter is passed by rvalue reference by the existing callers; treat it as a borrowed, immutable principal rather than assuming ownership is transferred. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classEntityController" kindref="compound">EntityController</ref>, <ref refid="classController" kindref="compound">Controller</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
